---
description: Backend standards for the Express API
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/API_CONTRACT.md`, `docs/DATA_MODEL.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md`, and `docs/SECURITY.md` before relevant changes.
- Organize code by domain module; keep routes/controllers thin.
- Validate route params, query strings, and bodies with Zod.
- Keep domain logic in services, not route handlers.
- Map known errors centrally to stable public error codes; never expose stack traces.
- Keep OpenAI SDK calls behind an infrastructure adapter.
- Provide a mock AI provider for tests; tests must not require network/API keys.
- Never calculate authoritative prices with an LLM or JavaScript floating-point arithmetic.
- Use configured currency/tax policy and decimal-safe money arithmetic.
- Snapshot product name/SKU/unit/price on quotation items.
- Agent-generated quotations start as DRAFT/PENDING_REVIEW.
- Approval/rejection must be a separate authorized use case.
- Add tests for success, validation failure, not-found, conflict, and provider failure as appropriate.
